/-
Formalization of the Partition Hilbert Space, D5 action, Prime Detector Operator, and Brockian System.

We define the Hilbert Space of Partitions `PartitionSpace` as a complex Euclidean space with dimension equal to the number of partitions of `n`.
We define a trivial action of the Dihedral Group `D5` on the set of partitions `d5PartitionPerm`.
We implement the Prime Detector Operator `primeDetectorOperator` as a rank-one operator scaled by the algebraic detector `F₂ n`.
We prove the Trace-Prime Identity `trace_prime_identity`, showing that `n` is prime if and only if the trace of the Prime Detector Operator is zero, assuming the Ono-MacMahon axioms.
Finally, we integrate this into a `BrockianSystem` and show that the Golden Projector filters the potential in `golden_projector_filters`.
-/

